---
// SEOContent — long-form on-page copy for search engines and readers.
// Woven around the primary keyword "home mortgage calculator" with
// supporting long-tail keywords. Rendered on the home page.
import { faqs } from '../data/faqs';
---

<section class="py-16 sm:py-24 bg-canvas border-t border-hairline">
  <div class="container-main max-w-3xl">
    <h2 class="text-ink font-semibold text-2xl sm:text-[32px] leading-tight tracking-[-1.28px] mb-4">
      What Our Free Home Mortgage Calculator Does
    </h2>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Buying a home is one of the biggest financial decisions you will ever make, and the
      numbers can feel overwhelming. Our <strong>free home mortgage calculator</strong> cuts through
      the confusion by showing you a realistic monthly payment in seconds. Instead of entering
      formulas by hand or getting rough lender estimates, you get a precise, real-time breakdown
      you can trust before you ever set foot in a bank.
    </p>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-6">
      Most people focus on just the list price, but your true monthly cost is made up of several
      parts. This <strong>house mortgage calculator</strong> rolls principal and interest, property
      taxes, homeowners insurance, private mortgage insurance (PMI), and HOA fees into a single
      total — giving you the clearest possible picture of what homeownership will actually cost.
    </p>
<h3 class="text-ink font-semibold text-xl tracking-tight mb-3 mt-8">
      How Your Monthly Payment Is Calculated
    </h3>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Mortgage lenders use a standard formula to determine how much you pay each month. It combines
      the loan amount, your interest rate, and the length of your loan term. Our monthly mortgage
      calculator applies that math instantly and then factors in every additional recurring cost:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-6">
      <li><strong>Principal &amp; interest</strong> — the core of your payment that pays down the loan and the borrowing cost.</li>
      <li><strong>Property taxes</strong> — typically collected monthly and held in escrow by your lender.</li>
      <li><strong>Homeowners insurance</strong> — protects your property against damage and liability.</li>
      <li><strong>PMI</strong> — required when your down payment is under 20%.</li>
      <li><strong>HOA fees</strong> — monthly dues if your community has a homeowners association.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="text-ink font-semibold text-xl tracking-tight mb-3 mt-8">
      Compare Loan Terms With the 30-Year Mortgage Calculator
    </h3>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
      The loan term you choose dramatically changes your payment. A <strong>30-year mortgage calculator</strong>
      shows how spreading your loan over three decades keeps payments affordable, while 15- and
      20-year terms build equity faster and save thousands in interest. Use the term toggle to
      compare monthly payments and total cost side by side.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-ink font-semibold text-xl tracking-tight mb-3 mt-8">
      Understand the Mortgage Calculator Amortization Schedule
    </h3>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
      With the built-in <strong>mortgage calculator amortization</strong> schedule, you can see exactly how
      each payment splits between principal and interest over the life of your loan. Early payments
      go mostly toward interest; later payments chip away at principal. Watching the balance drop
      month by month helps you plan, budget, and decide when refinancing makes sense.
    </p>
<h3 class="text-ink font-semibold text-xl tracking-tight mb-3 mt-8">
      Save With a Mortgage Calculator With Extra Payments
    </h3>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Paying a little extra each month can shorten your loan by years and save five figures in
      interest. Our <strong>mortgage calculator with extra payments</strong> lets you add any extra
      monthly amount and instantly shows your new payoff date and total interest saved. Whether it's
      biweekly payments, rounding up, or an annual lump sum, the numbers are just a few clicks away.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-ink font-semibold text-xl tracking-tight mb-3 mt-8">
      Is This A Good Refinance Mortgage Calculator?
    </h3>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-6">
      For that reason, it also works as a practical <strong>refinance mortgage calculator</strong>.
      Estimate your current payment, then adjust the interest rate and term to model a refi. If the
      new monthly payment (minus closing costs) improves your cash flow, you'll know whether
      refinancing is worth exploring with a lender.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-ink font-semibold text-xl tracking-tight mb-3 mt-8">
      Built for Buyers Everywhere, Including Texas
    </h3>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Property taxes and insurance vary widely by location. For buyers in high-tax states, a
      <strong>mortgage calculator Texas</strong> mindset is essential — local tax rates can add
      hundreds to a monthly payment. This tool makes it easy to enter your actual annual tax and
      insurance costs, so the estimate reflects your region, whether you're in Texas, California,
      Florida, or anywhere else in the U.S.
    </p>
<h3 class="text-ink font-semibold text-xl tracking-tight mb-3 mt-8">
      Beyond Conventional Loans
    </h3>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed mb-6">
      While built for standard purchase financing, the same monthly-payment logic applies to other
      scenarios. A <strong>VA mortgage calculator</strong> helps eligible veterans and service members
      model no-down-payment loans. A <strong>reverse mortgage calculator</strong> can help older
      homeowners think about tapping home equity. And investors comparing options might explore a
      <strong>commercial mortgage calculator</strong> for rental or business properties. Punch in the
      numbers and let the math do the talking.
    </p>

    <div class="border-t border-hairline pt-8 mt-8">
      <h3 id="faq" class="text-ink font-semibold text-lg tracking-tight mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
      <div class="space-y-3">
        {faqs.map((f) => (
          <details class="group border border-hairline rounded-lg bg-canvas overflow-hidden">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 cursor-pointer list-none px-5 py-4 text-ink font-medium text-base select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
              <span>{f.question}</span>
              <span class="shrink-0 text-body transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-body text-base leading-relaxed">
              {f.answer}
            </div>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 text-center">
      <a href="#calculator" class="btn-primary">Try the Calculator Now</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>